    "result_text": "The change is complete and the full test suite is green.\n\n## What I did\n\nThe `Owner` response already exposed a computed `displayName` field, so I followed that same pattern for `initials`:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `initials` string property to the `Owner` schema (next to `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field.\n\n2. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a MapStruct `@Mapping` that computes it:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" +\n   owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n   producing e.g. `\"J.S.\"` from `\"john\"`/`\"smith\"`.\n\n## Result\n\n`Cp06Tests.coreComputesInitials` passes, and the full suite is green: **Tests run: 12, Failures: 0, Errors: 0**, BUILD SUCCESS.\n\nNote: the field is derived from the first character of each name; the spec's examples all use single-word names, so I didn't special-case blank names (the request validation already rejects blank `firstName`/`lastName`, so both are guaranteed non-empty at response time).",
